s to run the greeter, its arguments\n52\t      included. Everything a user sees of the greeter follows from one.\n53\t  - term: exit code\n54\t    means: >-\n55\t      The number the command ends with: 0 when it succeeded, anything\n56\t      else when it did not. Scripts calling the greeter branch on it.\n57\t  - term: standard output\n58\t    means: >-\n59\t      The lines the command prints for its user, its answer and its log\n60\t      records alike. It is the greeter's only visible output.\n61\t\n62\tconcepts:\n63\t  given:\n64\t    - concept: configured greeting\n65\t      means: >-\n66\t        The project's config file sets the greeting to a stated text\n67\t        before the command runs.\n68\t      terms: [greeting, command]\n69\t  when:\n70\t    - concept: a role runs a command\n71\t      means: >-\n72\t        A role runs one stated command line once, in the project\n73\t        directory, and waits for it to exit.\n74\t      terms: [command]\n75\t  then:\n76\t    - concept: exit code\n77\t      means: >-\n78\t        The command the role ran ended with a stated exit code; 0 means\n79\t        it succeeded.\n80\t      terms: [command, exit code]\n81\t    - concept: standard output\n82\t      means: >-\n83\t        A line the command printed on its standard output has a match for\n84\t        a stated pattern, a regular expression.\n85\t      terms: [command, standard output]\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b20a4c2-e10c-4b10-b363-f740b510f9ef","uuid":"e11aa822-b951-4b37-9e0a-448a5c8547aa","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:09:45.682Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/docs/product/product.yaml","content":"# Product document for `scen-check-validation-fails`: the greeter, as\n# its other fixtures carry it.\n#\n# Its concepts cover E2E-002's steps, and the glossary defines every term\n# they declare. E2E-001's defective steps fall under none of them.\n\ntitle: \"Greeter\"\n\ndescription:\n  summary: >-\n    A command-